# Opt-in creds for the live testnet/mirrornet broadcast smoke
# (app/utils/__tests__/testnetBroadcast.smoke.test.ts).
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in. The smoke SKIPS unless NODE + ACCOUNT + at least one role
# key (ACTIVE or POSTING) are set; when set it broadcasts a balance-neutral custom_json (and, if MEMO
# is present, an encrypted-memo transfer) against the node and asserts a real hived accepts it.
#
# ⚠️ Use a THROWAWAY account. A posting/active key that works on Mirrornet is the SAME key that works on
#    mainnet for that account's ops — never put a valuable/real account's key here. A Mirrornet-only
#    account (created there, not on mainnet) is ideal: its key has zero mainnet value.

# Mirrornet mirrors mainnet on a separate chain_id (HIVE/HBD symbols, STM prefix). The smoke reads the
# real chain_id from the node's get_config and refuses a mainnet chain_id, so nothing is hardcoded.
VESSEL_TESTNET_NODE=https://api.fake.openhive.network
VESSEL_TESTNET_ACCOUNT=your-throwaway-account
VESSEL_TESTNET_ACTIVE=5Kxxxxxxxx-that-account-ACTIVE-wif
VESSEL_TESTNET_POSTING=5Kxxxxxxxx-that-account-POSTING-wif
VESSEL_TESTNET_MEMO=5Kxxxxxxxx-that-account-MEMO-wif
